       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nAcetaminophen 3000 mg three times daily comes to 9,000 mg/day. The usual adult maximum is 4,000 mg/day, and many institutions cap it at 3,000 mg/day. A single 3,000 mg dose is also well above the usual 500\u20131,000 mg per dose. This amount risks serious hepatotoxicity, even with normal liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **1,000 mg PO three times daily** (3,000 mg/day total)\n- **650 mg PO every 6 hours** (2,600 mg/day total)\n- **500\u20131,000 mg PO every 6\u20138 hours as needed**, not to exceed your institution's daily maximum\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. If you do want the original dose, tell me and I'll take that into account, but I'd advise checking with pharmacy first."
      }
