       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Acetaminophen 3000 mg three times daily is 9,000 mg/day, more than double the 4,000 mg/day maximum. I know of no indication that justifies it. It could cause acute liver failure, and normal liver function doesn't protect against that at this dose.\n\nHere's what I can do:\n- **Enter a standard dose right away.** For example, 1,000 mg PO three times daily (3,000 mg/day) or 1,000 mg PO every 8 hours. I can also use a different dose you choose within the safe range.\n- **Help you escalate.** If you're trying to reach a particular analgesic goal, such as for severe pain, I can enter a multimodal regimen instead. Pharmacy or your attending can help with the choice.\n- **Check for a typo.** If you meant 3,000 mg/day total or a different drug, tell me and I'll enter it.\n\nIf you believe there's a real clinical reason for this dose, please talk to pharmacy or your attending first. They can enter or override the order through the appropriate channels."
      }
